  "_readme": "WFG-129. Of the origins whose FIRE-BLIND route enters the forecast on the canonical Yeongdeok field, how many a PRESENT-PERIMETER-ONLY router already saves. The present-perimeter arm is slice 0 of the committed hazard field used as a node filter (prob_at(x, y, 0.0) >= p_cut, the same predicate candidate_origins uses to refuse a burning origin), then the repository's own naive_route over the filtered graph, SCORED against the full forecast exactly as the other two arms are. Zero buffer: this is NOT WFG-033(b). Read docs/present_perimeter_yeongdeok.md, section 5, before quoting any number here.",
